icant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUMORI, YOSHIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAI, KENICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAWAMOTO, NORIHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>STAR MICRONICS CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUKUDA, YASUNORI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUMORI YOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGAI KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAWAMOTO NORIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUKUDA YASUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUMORI, YOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAI, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAWAMOTO, NORIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUKUDA, YASUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A rotary printer (10) comprises a thermal print head (11) traveling in the principle feed direction or a radial direction of an endless or disk medium (M), and a stepping motor (15) for moving the disk medium (M) in the secondary feed direction or a circumferential direction of the disk medium (M). An image composed of a number of pixels arranged in radial and circumferential directions of the disk medium (M) is formed according to the image data supplied by an external host system. The printed area (Ra) corresponding to a predetermined length from the starting position (PS) of the thermal print head (11) coincides with the printed area (Rb) corresponding to a predetermined length to the end position (PE) of the head. Since the printed overlap is invisible, high print quality is achieved.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une imprimante rotative (10) qui comprend une tête d'impression thermique (11) dont le parcours s'effectue dans le sens d'alimentation principal ou dans un sens radial d'un support sans fin ou de disque (M), un moteur pas à pas (15) pour déplacer le support de disque (M) dans le sens d'alimentation secondaire ou dans un sens périphérique du support de disque (M). Une image constituée de plusieurs pixels disposés dans un sens radial et dans un sens périphérique du support de disque (M) est formée sur la base des données d'image fournies par un système hôte extérieur. La zone imprimée (Ra) correspondant à une longueur préétablie depuis la position de départ (PS) de la tête d'impression thermique (11) coincide avec la zone imprimée (Rb) correspondant à une longueur préétablie vers une position d'arrivée (PE) de la tête. Le recouvrement imprimé étant invisible, on obtient une impression de grande qualité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_lice